---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About — Brian J. Mueller"
      description="Poet, retreat co-leader, and Director of Education & Engagement for Choosing Presence. Twelve books of poetry from southwestern Ohio.">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="about-lead">
      <figure class="portrait">
        <img src="/img/brian-2021-640.webp"
             srcset="/img/brian-2021-320.webp 320w, /img/brian-2021-640.webp 640w"
             sizes="(max-width: 800px) 60vw, 18rem"
             width="640" height="640" alt="Brian J. Mueller" />
      </figure>

      <div class="stack stack-l">
        <div class="stack stack-m">
          <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
          <h1>Brian J. Mueller</h1>
          <hr class="rule-short" />
          <p class="lede">I write poems for everyone.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="stack stack-m">
          <p>My journey with poetry began between college lectures, but it truly took flight
             through the rhythm of my favourite songs and the landscapes of my travels. In 2002
             I published my first collection, <em>Bull Head</em>. Eleven volumes have followed.</p>

          <p>For five years I shared my work daily through <em>Brian's Poem of the Day</em>,
             from 2016 to 2020, and I picked the practice back up in 2023. Readers tell me they
             like that the writing is candid and easy to get into. I believe every one of us
             carries the voice and spirit of a poet. The real work is hearing that voice, and
             then having the nerve to share it.</p>

          <p>The daily poem turned into something larger: a request to design a writing retreat
             for men, built around healing and spiritual growth. I have now co-led that retreat
             for a decade. It continues each January as
             <a href="/retreat">Rooted in the Land</a>, and two of the books on this site —
             the <a href="/series/men-writing-for-change">Men Writing for Change</a> volumes —
             are not mine alone but the work of the men who came.</p>

          <p>I believe poetry is the language of the soul. It offers the depth and meaning we
             often crave, stirring our passions while anchoring us in the intuitive truth that
             there is always more to life than meets the eye. Among the poets I keep returning
             to are Rumi, Mary Oliver, Mark Nepo, Charles Bukowski and Wendell Berry.</p>

          <p>Away from the page, I serve as Director of Education &amp; Engagement for
             <a href="https://www.choosingpresence.org">Choosing Presence</a>, and I am an
             active member of the <a href="https://illuman.org/ohio">Ohio chapter of Illuman</a>,
             which supports men on their spiritual journeys. My books are published under my own
             imprint, Digital Alphabet Books.</p>

          <p>I live in southwestern Ohio with my wife and our dogs, who snooze and keep me
             company while I write.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn" href="/books">The books</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
